<h2>The case against the applicant</h2>
<p>On 5 April 2022, Customs officials intercepted the applicant at IGI Airport, New Delhi, on his arrival from Addis Ababa. He allegedly disclosed that he had ingested capsules containing narcotics. Six capsules were recovered at the airport and seventy-nine more at Dr. Ram Manohar Lohia Hospital — eighty-five in total, found to contain cocaine weighing about 1,088 grams, a commercial quantity under the NDPS Act. He was formally arrested on 10 April 2022. The prosecution complaint was filed on 6 October 2022 and charges were framed on 17 March 2023 in SC No. 786/2022, under Sections 21(c) and 23(c) of the NDPS Act.</p>
<table class="law">
